{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-brings-riemann-hurwitz","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:brings-riemann-hurwitz","kind":"lemma","title":"Riemann--Hurwitz count for a degree-4 covering $\\Sigma_4 \\to \\mathbb{P}^1$","proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-brings-riemann-hurwitz"],"tags":["riemann-hurwitz","ramification","brings-surface","s5-symmetry"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.brings_riemann_hurwitz","text":"brings-riemann-hurwitz.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:brings-riemann-hurwitz\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi \\colon \\Sigma_4 \\to \\mathbb{P}^1</code> be a branched covering of degree <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code> from a genus-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code> curve onto the projective line. Its total ramification is fixed by the Riemann--Hurwitz formula:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  R_{\\mathrm{tot}}\n  = 2g(\\Sigma_4) - 2 - 4(2g(\\mathbb{P}^1) - 2)\n  = 6 + 8\n  = 14.</code></pre>\n<p><em>The existence of such a covering, and the claim that its branch locus has exactly <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6</code> points, are hypotheses of this lemma, not consequences of it.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-riemann-hurwitz.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"8.4.13","page":"b/lem-brings-riemann-hurwitz","qa":{"counts":{"pass":93,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.brings_riemann_hurwitz","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/brings_riemann_hurwitz.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
